        {
          "title": "Femkort",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Femkort is a Swedish last-trick card game where the final trick is decisive and the ace of hearts can win the pot."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Femkort, meaning Five Cards, is a Swedish member of the last-trick group related to Agram, Chicago, Letzter Stich, and Toepen. Its short five-minute deals focus attention on timing the final trick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "3-8 players use the table arrangement described for Femkort."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52-card French-suited Swedish Modern pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "52-card French-suited Swedish Modern pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal 52-card French-suited Swedish Modern pack for 3-8 players according to the local rules before the first trick."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
